      "name": "p_marketeer",
      "op": "CONST_STR",
      "attributes": {
        "value": "You are the MARKETEER for plan: apxm-designer\n\nFind the money: THE BUYER (who writes the check \u2014 not the user), THE PAIN (how much does this cost them today), THE SWITCH (why 10x better, not 10%), FIRST 10 (who are first 10 customers, how to find them), PRICING (model + price point that makes sense).\n\nOutput 400-600 words with headers. Be specific.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500 PLAN \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n# apxm-designer \u2014 AI-First Commercial App Builder on APXM\n\n## What Is apxm-designer?\n\nYou describe an app in plain language. apxm-designer produces a production-ready application \u2014 frontend + backend + tests \u2014 for any tech stack.\n\nThe gap every existing tool leaves: Tools like Replit Agent and Firebase Studio skip the design phase entirely. They go straight to code. What you get is whatever the AI decided in context: missing empty states, inconsistent components across screens, undocumented interaction decisions. You discover the gaps in QA or production.\n\napxm-designer's answer: a structured, enforced design phase \u2014 ALL screens \u00d7 ALL states, designed in verified HTML, human-approved \u2014 before a single line of implementation code is written. The HTML IS the design AND the spec AND the conversion source. One artifact, no translation, no drift.\n\n## The 5 Architectural Innovations\n\n1. HTML as Universal Intermediate Format \u2014 one format, five consumers (browser, Playwright, Qwen3, Qwen-VL, sub/convert.apxm), zero translation\n2. The Verification Gate \u2014 Stage 1 (Qwen3 structural) + Stage 2 (Qwen-VL visual) BLOCK implementation if they fail\n3. Component Registry as Single Source of Truth \u2014 component_registry.json drives HTML, Figma, Code Connect, and framework widgets\n4. File-per-State Maps to State Machine \u2014 dashboard.html, dashboard-triage.html, dashboard-empty.html \u2192 DashboardState.loaded/triage/empty\n5. Figma as Optional Shareable View \u2014 Figma is OUTPUT (never authoritative source), generated from verified HTML\n\n## The Full Pipeline\n\n```\nPHASE 1: DISCOVER (4 parallel specialists)\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 Entity + State Machine Analyst (CLAUDE REASON) \u2192 entity_map.json\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 Competitor + Market Analyst (GEMINI) \u2192 competitor_analysis.json\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 IA + Navigation Analyst (CLAUDE THINK) \u2192 navigation_spec.json\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 Design Style Analyst (GEMINI) \u2192 design_system.json\n    \u2502\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500 Q&A \u00b7 3 ROUNDS \u2192 6 spec artifacts\n        \u2502\n        \u251c\u2500\u2500 Architect writes specs\n        \u2514\u2500\u2500 Adversary challenges (wins on scope disputes)\n    \u2502\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500 \ud83d\udc64 APPROVE\n\nPHASE 2A: Common Parts (components)\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 component_registry.json \u2192 N components in parallel\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 CODEX (conservative) + CLAUDE (bold) \u2192 CLAUDE picks winner\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 2-stage verification on components\n\nPHASE 2B: Common Screens (shared across features)\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 profile, messaging, settings\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 Uses common parts, same verification\n\nPHASE 2C: Feature Screens (N screens \u00d7 V variants, ALL IN PARALLEL)\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 capabilities/seller/home/dashboard.html\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 capabilities/seller/home/dashboard-triage.html\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 capabilities/seller/home/dashboard-empty.html\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 Each uses [data-component] placeholders\n\n2-STAGE VERIFICATION:\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 Stage 1: Qwen3 structural (reads ALL HTML text at once)\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 Stage 2: Playwright \u2192 PNG \u2192 Qwen-VL visual review\n\nPHASE 3A: CONVERT (HTML \u2192 framework code)\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 Step 1: Widget generation (per component)\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 Step 2: Screen conversion (per HTML file)\n\nPHASE 3B: IMPLEMENT (wiring + backend)\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 Backend: CODEX \u00d7 N endpoint groups\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 Wiring: CLAUDE (routing, state, DI, i18n, auth)\n\nPHASE 4: TEST\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 Stack tests \u2192 Qwen3 coverage audit \u2192 CLAUDE quality gate\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 REFLECT \u2192 UMEM(LTM cache) \u2192 update state.json \u2192 DONE\n```\n\n## Competitive Position\n\n| Tool | \"Design Step\" | Output |\n|---|---|---|\n| Figma | Human draws each screen | Picture (disconnected from code) |\n| Replit Agent | Text paragraph | Running React app (missing states) |\n| Firebase Studio | Text outline | React/Next.js (same problem) |\n| Bolt/v0 | None | React+Tailwind (one screen at a time) |\n| Google Stitch | None | HTML+CSS (one screen, no state variants, no verification) |\n| **apxm-designer** | 4 specialists \u2192 6 artifacts \u2192 N\u00d7V verified HTML | Verified HTML \u2192 Figma (opt) \u2192 any framework |\n\nWhen Replit wins: Simple apps (<10 screens, MVP, speed is only goal)\nWhen apxm-designer wins: Complex apps (20+ screens, multiple audiences, many states, multi-platform)\n\n## Key Artifacts\n\n- product_spec.json \u2014 what the app does\n- screen_manifest.json \u2014 all screens \u00d7 all variants with components_used\n- component_registry.json \u2014 single source of truth for components\n- interaction_map.json \u2014 data-action/destination mappings\n- stack_config.json \u2014 framework + backend + auth\n- design_system.json \u2014 CSS variables, typography, spacing\n\n## CLI Interface\n\n```bash\napxm-designer create \"A marketplace for handmade crafts\" --stack flutter --backend go\napxm-designer add-feature \"Add a review system\" --project ./my-marketplace\napxm-designer edit-screen seller/home/dashboard --project ./my-marketplace\napxm-designer verify --project ./my-marketplace\napxm-designer figma-sync --project ./my-marketplace --file-key Yl6T9eQJNU8\n```\n\n## APXM Workflow Files\n\n| File | Phase | Description |\n|------|-------|-------------|\n| create.apxm | Entry | Full app from scratch |\n| add-feature.apxm | Entry | Feature delta \u2014 2C + 3 + 4 |\n| phases/discover.apxm | 1 | Discovery + Q&A + spec |\n| phases/common-parts.apxm | 2A | Component library |\n| phases/feature-screens.apxm | 2C | Feature screens |\n| sub/screen.apxm | atomic | One file: conservative + bold + pick |\n| sub/verify-structural.apxm | atomic | Qwen3 audit |\n| sub/verify-visual.apxm | atomic | Playwright \u2192 Qwen-VL |\n| sub/convert.apxm | atomic | HTML \u2192 framework screen |\n\n## The Honest Trade-off\n\napxm-designer is SLOWER than Replit for simple apps (by design \u2014 design phase comes first).\napxm-designer is MORE COMPLETE than any tool for complex apps.\nThe design phase makes the unknowns known BEFORE implementation.\n"
      }
    },
